course: dictionary
lesson: 3452
title: A word for a short craze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things are popular for a little while and then nobody wants them any more. The word for these is fad. Read the clues in this sentence: «Jack spends his whole £10 on the fidget toy everyone has, and two days later nobody cares about fidget toys any more.» The words everyone has and two days later nobody cares show that the craze was big and then went quickly.
explain: So a fad is something, like a toy, game, fashion or food, that becomes very popular suddenly and is then quickly forgotten. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "Fidget toys were a fad" makes sense, because they were popular and then forgotten.
explain: A fad diet is a popular way of eating that promises quick results but is often not healthy. Adults might say, «It's just a fad», to mean something will not last. Be careful: a diet on its own is just a way of eating. It is a fad only when it is a short-lived craze.
fact: Fad is a noun: a fad, fads.
fact: «Fad» means something, like a toy, game, fashion or food, that becomes very popular suddenly and is then quickly forgotten.
fact: A fad is another word for a short-lived craze.
fact: A «fad diet» is a popular way of eating that promises quick results but is often not healthy.
fact: A diet means eating less or differently to lose weight or feel healthier; some diets are sensible and some are fads that do not last.
exercise: Jack spends his whole £10 on the fidget toy everyone has, and two days later nobody cares about fidget toys any more. What kind of thing is the fidget toy craze? | A fashion that lasts for many years | A healthy kind of diet | *A fad that became popular suddenly and was then forgotten | A school rule about toys
exercise: Which of these is a fad diet? | A plan for school dinners | A way of eating that is sensible and healthy for years | *A popular way of eating that promises quick results but is often not healthy | A list of healthy foods from a doctor
exercise: Nadia says, «It's just a fad.» What does she mean about the game? | It will be healthy and last for years | *It will be popular for a short time, then be forgotten | It is a very old game from the past | It is a new kind of food
test: «I wonder what new fad he has taken up now?» What does fad mean here? | A kind of old castle | A quiet, sad feeling | A long, healthy habit | *A short craze that is popular for a while
test: Which is most likely to be a fad? | Your own birthday | A grandad's favourite old armchair | The weather in autumn | *A loom band craze that everybody wants for a month
exam: Mia says, «Not every food tip is a fad: sensible advice lasts.» What is a fad here? | *A food tip that becomes popular suddenly and is then quickly forgotten | A dreich, grey day | Advice that everyone follows for years | Something that is ancient
